IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 6: SUPPLEMENTAL (s 70).
-- Section 70 converts actions and applications that were commenced by petition and are still pending when a written law is amended to require a writ of summons or an originating summons.
-- It could be read as a saving provision (inert, reason 2); it is encoded instead, because it gives a court a power over pending proceedings.

§ `Section 70 -- conversion of pending petitions`

-- src:2382 | 70.—(1) Where —
-- src:2384 | (a) under any written law any civil action or application may
-- src:2385 | be commenced in or made to a District Court, a
-- src:2386 | Magistrate’s Court or the registrar (called in this section
-- src:2387 | the Court); and
-- src:2389 | (b) the provisions under any written law by virtue of which
-- src:2390 | such an action or application was required to be
-- src:2391 | commenced or made by way of a petition have been
-- src:2392 | amended such as to require that any such action or
-- src:2393 | application must, as from the date appointed for the
-- src:2394 | coming into operation of the amendment, be commenced
-- src:2395 | or made by way of a writ of summons or an originating
-- src:2396 | summons,
-- src:2398 | then, if any such action or application that has been commenced or
-- src:2399 | made before that date by way of a petition is still pending before the
-- src:2400 | Court on or after that date, the Court may, if it thinks just and
-- src:2401 | expedient, order that the action or application (called in this section a
-- src:2402 | pending action or application) be converted to and be continued as an
-- src:2403 | action or application commenced or made by way of a writ of
-- src:2404 | summons or an originating summons, as is appropriate.
@ref s 70(1)(a) and (b) (src:2382-2404)
GIVEN `under a written law a civil action or application may be commenced in or made to a District Court, a Magistrate's Court or the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions requiring commencement by petition have been amended so as to require a writ of summons or an originating summons from the date appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application was commenced or made by way of a petition before that date and is still pending before the Court on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks it just and expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(1) the Court may order the pending action or application to be converted and continued by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — (a) ...; and (b) ..., then, if any such action or application that has been commenced or made before that date by way of a petition is still pending before the Court on or after that date, the Court may" (a "where" or "if" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF NOT (`under a written law a civil action or application may be commenced in or made to a District Court, a Magistrate's Court or the registrar` AND `the provisions requiring commencement by petition have been amended so as to require a writ of summons or an originating summons from the date appointed` AND `the action or application was commenced or made by way of a petition before that date and is still pending before the Court on or after that date`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Court thinks it just and expedient` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it thinks just and expedient"; the judgment is the Court's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2406 | (2) The Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of
-- src:2407 | the Chief Justice, may, where the Presiding Judge considers it
-- src:2408 | necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of
-- src:2409 | justice, by order direct that any class or description of pending actions
-- src:2410 | or applications before the Court be converted to and be continued as
-- src:2411 | actions or applications commenced or made by way of a writ of
-- src:2412 | summons or an originating summons, as is appropriate.
@ref s 70(2) (src:2406-2412)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `the Chief Justice concurs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge considers it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may by order direct that a class or description of pending actions or applications be converted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "The Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice"
        IF NOT (holder EQUALS `Presiding Judge of the State Courts`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice concurs` AND `the Presiding Judge considers it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, may, where the Presiding Judge considers it necessary or expedient" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2416 | (3) Where pursuant to subsection (1) or (2) any pending action or
-- src:2417 | application has been converted to an action or application
-- src:2422 | commenced or made by way of a writ of summons or an originating
-- src:2423 | summons —
-- src:2425 | (a) the action or application is to be continued in accordance
-- src:2426 | with the provisions of the relevant written law and the
-- src:2427 | practice and procedure as are in force and applicable in
-- src:2428 | relation to that action or application at the time of the
-- src:2429 | conversion; and
@ref s 70(3)(a) (src:2416-2429)
GIVEN `a pending action or application has been converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(3)(a) the converted action or application is continued in accordance with the relevant written law and the practice and procedure in force at the time of the conversion` MEANS
    IF `a pending action or application has been converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where pursuant to subsection (1) or (2) any pending action or application has been converted ..., (a) the action or application is to be continued in accordance with ..." (this paragraph gives no continuation on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:2416 | (3) Where pursuant to subsection (1) or (2) any pending action or
-- src:2417 | application has been converted to an action or application
-- src:2422 | commenced or made by way of a writ of summons or an originating
-- src:2423 | summons —
-- src:2431 | (b) the Court may give to the parties to the action or
-- src:2432 | application such directions as to the conduct and costs of
-- src:2433 | the action or application as it thinks just and expedient for
-- src:2434 | the purpose of facilitating the conversion of the action or
-- src:2435 | application to an action or application commenced or made
-- src:2436 | by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons
-- src:2437 | (as the case may be) and its continuance as such.
@ref s 70(3)(b) (src:2416-2437)
GIVEN `a pending action or application has been converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks the directions just and expedient for the purpose of facilitating the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(3)(b) the Court may give the parties directions as to the conduct and costs of the action or application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where pursuant to subsection (1) or (2) any pending action or application has been converted ..., (b) the Court may give to the parties ... such directions" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF NOT (`a pending action or application has been converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Court thinks the directions just and expedient for the purpose of facilitating the conversion` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as it thinks just and expedient"; the judgment is the Court's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
